  "notes": "{差|さ}し{支|つか}える is commonly used in polite conditional expressions.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- お{差|さ}し{支|つか}えなければ: if it's not inconvenient (polite)\n- {差|さ}し{支|つか}えない: no problem, fine\n- 〜に{差|さ}し{支|つか}える: to interfere with ~\n\nRELATED NOUN:\n{差|さ}し{支|つか}え: hindrance, obstacle\n- {差|さ}し{支|つか}えがある: there is a problem\n- {差|さ}し{支|つか}えがない: no problem",
